    "created_at": "2023-03-03T11:49:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-03T11:49:35Z",
    "body": "They can, actually. As long as it is between repositories for the same organisation. This is better than reopening a new issue as it makes sure all links continue working (and preserves history and such). We do this quite a bit for the noVNC project.\r\n\r\nThat said, since uievents is not hosted by @whatwg, but rather by @w3c, it would not work in this case.\r\n\r\nI've now opened https://github.com/w3c/uievents/issues/343 over there. Thanks.",
